e4-9d2b3a2979a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111525 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111531 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111525 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111531 #edb/ref 1061 17999 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111531 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8150e1a1-0f41-5dc7-a1db-5e474331d638" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111531 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111884 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's recap some of the rules for exponents.\n\n- **Product rule**: to multiply powers of the same base, add the exponents.\n\n- **Quotient rule**: to divide powers of the same base, subtract the exponents.\n\n- **Power rule**: to raise a power to another power, multiply the exponents.\n\n- **Power of product rule**: to raise the product of two numbers to a power, raise each number to that power, and then multiply.\n\n- **Power of quotient rule**: to raise a fraction to a power, raise both the numerator and the denominator to that power.\n\nWe can use a combination of these rules to simplify expressions containing exponents. Let's see an example of this." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111884 #edb/ref 1065 3275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111884 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7c442391-b257-5c16-9fe0-292a45e3c172" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111884 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115224 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115224 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115224 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115224 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488224 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115224 #edb/ref 1039 "Ordering the Angles of a Triangle by Size Given the Sides" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115224 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186115054 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115224 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "676e3d29-f6fa-5fe4-aae4-e9c0e974ee74" #edb/ref 17592186045417] 