92186045417] [17592186180335 #edb/ref 1061 952859 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180335 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8792ecc7-4ffa-5de3-b84a-5c51e5d91d42" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180335 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179641 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180781 #edb/ref 1064 "When solving a multivariable equation for a particular variable, we sometimes have to factor some terms in the equation to reach the solution.\n\nFor example, let's solve the following equation for the variable $d\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n2cd - 3d = 5\n$$\n\nFirst, we factor out $d$ in the expression on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\nd(2c-3) = 5.\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $(2c-3)$ to isolate $d\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(2c-3) & =5 \\\\ \\frac{d(2c-3)}{2c-3} & =\\frac{5}{2c-3} \\\\ \\frac{d\\cancel{(2c-3)}}{\\cancel{2c-3}} & =\\frac{5}{2c-3} \\\\ d & =\\frac{5}{2c-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** This result assumes that $2c-3\\neq 0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180781 #edb/ref 1065 8665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180781 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "46409ede-9b62-5196-b665-c5ba29062b0d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180781 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192634 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048267 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192634 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193128 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192634 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193245 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192634 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186487339 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192634 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186487365 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192634 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186487368 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192634 #edb/ref 1039 "Isolating an Absolute Value Expression" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192634 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186192592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192634 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "5bc2c576-4f7c-5b4a-8c78-8a41420fdcce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192635 #edb/ref 